      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Five cases of renal angiomyolipoma which underwent spontaneous rupture are described. These patients presented as an \"acute abdomen\" for which the diagnosis was not initially apparent. A high index of suspicion is required to make the diagnosis even with modern imaging techniques. The treatment of these tumours is discussed."},
